expenses incurred in providing the services to ZenaTech. The agreement has a 20-year term. However, the agreement may be terminated at any time with the mutual consent of the parties. All funds due from Epazz, Inc. represent advances for programming, support, management fees, drone research and development on the statement of net income or loss. Epazz assists the Company through its drone facility in Pakistan.","context":"Management Services Agreement","section":"Business combinations and transactions under common control","block":555,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000616","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-24","reportDate":"2026-09-24","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000616/zt_ex99z1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/da80f95fb7e33bafc6cc705d8886fcd23502a51fe1d9dd16ed11eed803d44252.bin","sha256":"da80f95fb7e33bafc6cc705d8886fcd23502a51fe1d9dd16ed11eed803d44252"}},{"id":"f2b5936a4f7a91c00cbc0a5ebf18cb5ffcfd1c9469303f5dc1e6b68f5e13063e","quote":"·The Company acquired Velocity Geomatics, Inc., doing business as Velocity Group, Grande Prairie, Alberta, Canada on July 16, 2026, with operations and offices across Alberta, British Columbia and Saskatchewan. The acquisition marks ZenaTech’s first acquisition in drone-based geomatics for environmental and regulatory compliance and services in the oil and gas industry.","context":"(a) Acquisitions completed after June 30, 2026.","section":"Business combinations and transactions under common control","block":586,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000616","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-24","reportDate":"2026-09-24","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000616/zt_ex99z1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/da80f95fb7e33bafc6cc705d888